  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT. Code, repro and matcher outcomes all hold as filed.\nCODE: ruby.py ~2448-2461 (the WI-rijij/WI-mafik constant-receiver fallback): bare_class = receiver_class.lstrip(\":\"), a \"::\" receiver is cut to its LAST segment (rsplit(\"::\",1)[-1]), then require_hints.get(...) else bare_class.lower(). The lowercase heuristic dates from be0ddcb8eb (2026-05-12); WI-johib's ruby commits (2165b45f5a, 66608925db, 88ccd2e515, 09-28) changed the project-symbol lookup, not this slot.\nREPRO (scratch fixtures, survey, fresh cache), with and without require 'net/http':\n  Net::HTTP.get(URI(u)) -> ruby:http:0-0:get:external_symbol, dst_ref.module_path 'http', call_construct method, receiver constant_external\n  File.write(p, s) -> ruby:file:0-0:write:external_symbol\n  ::Net::HTTP.get(...) -> the same edge (call_lines [2, 4]), so the ::-rooted shape is covered by the same defect.\nMATCHER (python -c, io_boundary._module_matches(c, 'http')): Net::HTTP False, net::http True, net/http True, HTTP True, http True -- identical to the filing.\nCONSUMERS of the lowercase spelling: no built-in io_primitives/ruby.yaml exists (ruby rows come only from overlays); verify_claims.py ~3635 docstring cites ruby:http:0-0:new:external_symbol as analyzer output (text only); receiver_blind_magnets.py ~79 and axis_meta_keys.py ~483 key on the meta value constant_external, not on the slot spelling. Not checked: community overlays outside packages/*/src, and frameworks/*.yaml.\nADR-0051 §1 (owner path \"spelled in the source language's import vocabulary\") supports the item's \"the analyzer is wrong\" reading.\nAdjacent, not in scope: per ADR-0059 a call on the constant itself (Net::HTTP.get, File.write) is function-kind, yet the edge is stamped call_construct=method. WI-kazut (P3) is the binding-side sibling (Prometheus::Client short-name capture), already cross-referenced from WI-kazut."  # 744c
